The legal text is the Colorado Revised Statutes 2022 as released by the Office of Legislative Legal Services of the
Colorado General Assembly, read from Public.Resource.Org's Internet Archive item gov.co.crs.bulk
(https://archive.org/details/gov.co.crs.bulk), release r83.2023.06.

Public.Resource.Org marks that item with the Public Domain Mark 1.0 (http://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/mark/1.0/)
and describes it: "These are edicts of government and are thus the property of the people and not subject to
copyright. This law is your law." Its "Official State Codes" collection states: "The authentic exposition and
interpretation of the law, which, binding every citizen, is free for publication to all" (Banks v. Manchester,
128 U.S. 244 (1888)). Statute text is not copyrightable in the United States (Georgia v. Public.Resource.Org, Inc.,
590 U.S. 255 (2020)). Source notes, annotations and editor's notes are not included.

Changes made by Lexifina: one Markdown file per section, one paragraph per line, normalised spaces, quotation marks and
dashes; source notes, annotations, editor's notes, repealed sections and sections not in force on 10 August 2022 left
out. The wording of the law was not changed. Neither the Colorado General Assembly nor Public.Resource.Org endorses
this repository.

Lexifina's own contributions (the arrangement of the history, the commit messages, the tables and the tools) are
dedicated to the public domain under CC0 1.0 Universal: https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/legalcode
